 "status": "Seed list (Task 045b). Navin adds words: put them in 'words' and bump the version.",
 "source": "Navin, 23 October 2026: narration is mixed script; a Hindi word NOT in this list of simple everyday words gets its English word in brackets right after it, for example 'सतह (surface)'; subtitles show the bracket, the voice says 'सतह, यानी surface'.",
 "how_it_is_used": [
  "bie/brain/hinglish.py compares every Devanagari word of a script beat with this list after removing a common ending (ों, ें, ते, ता, ेंगे, ...). A word not found must be followed by its English word in brackets.",
  "Nukta and chandrabindu are ignored when comparing (ज़रा = जरा, आँख = आंख).",
  "English words in Roman script are never checked against this list and never have to be written in Devanagari."
 ],
